  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough. Every exfiltration path ends in exfiltrate_db or exfiltrate_fileserver. These need admin_db or admin_fileserver, which need foothold_db or foothold_fileserver, which need stolen_dbadmin. The only source of stolen_dbadmin is dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc. admin_dc comes only from escalate_dc, which needs foothold_dc. foothold_dc comes only from auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin. So deploying mfa:admin makes exfiltration impossible. Zero controls is not enough, because with no defences this path works: phish_workstation, pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db, exfiltrate_db. The minimum is therefore 1."
